{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>האמור</b> — The matter is this, that it is said in plain language: <b>אתם בית יעקב</b> ('You, O house of Jacob')?! And Rabbi Yeshuah said: It is as if he wrote שמע אתה הקרוא בית יעקב ('Hear, you who are called the house of Jacob'), and because of the alef, which is one of the guttural letters, the heh comes with a small patach, like <b>החזק הוא הרפה</b>." "<b>הקצר רוח השם</b> — This is prophecy. And the meaning: Does the spirit of HaShem not forever speak truth, for why would HaShem do evil?!" "<b>אם אלה מעלליו</b> — Is it His way to do evil to His creatures for nothing?! Rather, He speaks to benefit you, and good comes together with one who walks a straight path. And the meaning: His good word is fulfilled together with their deeds — if they are good."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The cross-reference is to 1 Samuel 4:7–8; Ibn Ezra there discusses the same phenomenon of heh with patach before a guttural."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:46.085877842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}